# {{ app_display_name }}

Compose Multiplatform app for Android{% if include_desktop %}, iOS and desktop{% else %} and iOS{% endif %}, generated from
[compose-multiplatform-cookie-cutter-template](https://github.com/alpenraum/compose-multiplatform-cookie-cutter-template).

## Getting started

```bash
./gradlew :androidApp:assembleDebug          # Android
./gradlew testAndroidHostTest               # unit tests (JVM)
{%- if include_desktop %}
./gradlew :composeApp:run                    # desktop
{%- endif %}
```

iOS: open `iosApp/iosApp.xcodeproj` in Xcode (Apple Silicon Mac required). For signing on a device, create
`iosApp/Configuration/Local.xcconfig` (gitignored) containing `TEAM_ID=<your team id>`.
{%- if include_networking %}

The backend base URL comes from BuildKonfig (`composeApp/build.gradle.kts`, `buildkonfig { }`).
Builds use the production URL unless you pass `-Pbuildkonfig.flavor=dev`.
{%- endif %}

## Structure

| Path | Contents |
|---|---|
| `composeApp/src/commonMain` | Shared code: `base/` (architecture, DI, errors, logging), `ui/`, `usecase/`, `data/` |
| `composeApp/src/androidMain`, `iosMain`{% if include_desktop %}, `desktopMain`{% endif %} | `actual` implementations{% if include_desktop %} and the desktop entry point{% endif %} |
| `androidApp` | Android entry point: `MainActivity`, `Application`, manifest, launcher icon, release config |
{%- if include_persistence %}
| `composeApp/db-schemas` | Exported Room schemas — commit them (see the README inside) |
{%- endif %}
{%- if include_library_module %}
| `{{ library_module_name }}` | Kotlin Multiplatform library used by `composeApp` |
{%- endif %}
| `iosApp` | Xcode project |
| `docs/conventions.md` | Project rules — read before changing code |

Version: Android and desktop read `version.properties`; iOS reads `iosApp/Configuration/Config.xcconfig`.
{%- if include_sonar %}

Code analysis: `SONAR_TOKEN=... ./sonar_scan.sh` ({{ sonar_host_url }}).
{%- endif %}

## Template updates

```bash
copier update     # needs a clean git working tree
```

Optional parts were chosen when the project was generated. Switching one off later via
`copier update` deletes its files including your edits — remove it by hand instead. Switching one
on adds its code, but this README, `CLAUDE.md` and `docs/conventions.md` are yours after the first
copy and are not updated.
